{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/18028-binary-thinking-solars-and-you","id":18028,"title":"Binary Thinking, Solars and YOU!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-25T16:50:41-08:00","id":18028,"title":"Binary Thinking, Solars and YOU!","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/332-most-exciting-new-3e-splat?p=6503#post6503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You seem to think a fuzzed definition is tantamount to having no means at all of discerning an Exalt from something else. Stop thinking in binary. I opened the definition to some non-standard ideas, not to &quot;just anything&quot; arbitrarily defined.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve been meaning to make a post about the utility of binary thinking for a while, but I\u2019ve never quite reached the right balance between motivation and boredom until now. It\u2019s come up a few times, most recently in the post I quoted above, and I think the number one problem with binary thinking around here isn\u2019t that people are thinking in binaries, but that they are not constructing the proper binaries to understand how Exalted is constructed as a setting and a set of mechanics.<br /> <br /> All thinking is fundamentally binary \u2013 a thing is itself and not any other thing. The trick is defining what the thing is and what it isn\u2019t and determining how a thing is marked as itself and not any other thing. In other words, how do you define the binary distinction?<br /> <br /> As an example, I\u2019ll use Solars.<br /> <br /> Distinction 1: Exalted/UnExalted<br /> <br /> The fundamental distinction, the distinction that the game is named after, is that of the Exalted and the UnExalted. All other distinctions \u2013 between splats, castes and individual Exalts \u2013 are based on this distinction. This also means that the distinction between the Exalted and the UnExalted has nothing to do with any characteristics of any of the splats. A third soul? Chosen of the gods? The craftsmanship of Autochthon? All of that is completely irrelevant to the distinction between the Exalted and the UnExalted.<br /> <br /> So how do you establish the distinction between the Exalted and the UnExalted? The books call them Exalted. That\u2019s it. You will never, ever find any other definition of the Exalted (unless John and Holden want to rupture the concept of Exaltation and cause most of the splats to collapse as the distinctions that define them are removed so that all splats can be defined simply as Exalted based on common criteria that differentiate them from the UnExalted, but I\u2019m pretty sure that\u2019s not going to happen).<br /> <br /> But that\u2019s all out-of-character information. In-character, Exaltation is self-produced, self-recognized and self-declared. The Exalted are Exalted because they consider themselves to be so and announce their Exaltation to the world. The state of Exaltation is intrinsic to the character and cannot be attributed to external forces, or else Exaltation would no longer be self-produced.<br /> <br /> (That some Exalted are chosen or constructed by a seemingly external force is not necessarily problematic to this definition. It simply means that the process of selection is intrinsic to the Exalted herself. I might make another post about this once I\u2019ve spent more time thinking it through.)<br /> <br /> This self-declaration stems from the Exalted\u2019s observations of the UnExalted and of the differences between themselves and the UnExalted. There are points of similarity between the Exalted and the UnExalted, but they are irrelevant. Only the differences matter, namely, that the Exalted are Exalted and that the UnExalted are not. The tautology is quite intentional and unavoidable.<br /> <br /> So that\u2019s the distinction that defines the Exalted and the UnExalted. Next up:<br /> <br /> Distinction 2: Solar/Exalted<br /> <br /> This distinction was a theoretical nightmare for me, because it\u2019s impossible for the Exalted to be distinguished from both the UnExalted and the Solars. It would no longer be a binary if it were.<br /> <br /> Which is why Solars (along with all the other splats) and the Exalted are two independent concepts.<br /> <br /> Exaltation as a concept defines itself in relation to the UnExalted. This means that it is incapable of defining itself in relation to Solars. In fact, because the Solars are Exalted, Exaltation is incapable of recognizing them as Solars. It would only ever refer to them as Exalted because the concept of Solars is unnecessary to the concept of the Exalted.<br /> <br /> However, the concept of the Exalted, which is inclusive of all splats, is necessary to the concept of Solars, as it allows Solars to define themselves and differentiate themselves from all other Exalted splats by using a single point of reference \u2013 a binary distinction. All Exalted are Exalted, but only Solars represent 1) the pursuit of human excellence 2) through the aesthetics of the Unconquered Sun 3) in a manner that defines the upper boundary of Exalted power.<br /> <br /> None of these three points are definitive of the Exalted as a broad concept (only the fact that they are Exalted is), so they create a distinction between Solars and the Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe pursuit of human excellence,\u201d which is generally taken to mean ability-based powers, differentiates Solars from splats that don\u2019t use ability-based powers.<br /> <br /> \u201cThrough the aesthetics of the Unconquered Sun\u201d differentiates Solars from other splats that use ability-based charms, but that are based on different aesthetics (Abyssals, Infernals, Sidereals, Dragon-Blooded, etc.).<br /> <br /> \u201cIn a manner that defines the upper boundary of Exalted power\u201d isn\u2019t really necessary as far as defining the splats go, but it does further differentiates Solars from everyone but Abyssals and Infernals (assuming they also operate at the upper boundary of Exalted power).<br /> <br /> So if there was some other splat that wasn\u2019t called Solars, but that represented the pursuit of human excellence through the aesthetics of the Unconquered Sun in a manner that defines the upper boundary of Exalted power, you would have to call them Solars because they would be functionally identical to Solars in every way (unless you added a fourth criteria of distinction which I can\u2019t think of right now).<br /> <br /> (As an aside, this is why superficial comparisons between Liminals and Abyssals or Getimians and Sidereals are pointless. Liminals are not defined in relation to Abyssals, nor are Getimians defined in relation to Sidereals. In any case, similarities are never relevant because, by their very nature, they can\u2019t be used to define anything. Only differences matter.)<br /> <br /> Which leads to:<br /> <br /> Distinction 3: Caste/Solar<br /> <br /> Actually five distinctions: Dawn/Solar, Zenith/Solar, Twilight/Solar, Night/Solar and Eclipse/Solar.<br /> <br /> Much of what I said about Solars and their relation to the Exalted also applies here. The concept of Solars includes all five Castes, so it cannot recognize the five Castes as discrete concepts. The Castes only exist because they differentiate themselves from Solars and, in doing so, from all the other existing Castes.<br /> <br /> Solars represent the pursuit of human excellence through the aesthetics of the Unconquered Sun in a manner that defines the upper boundary of Exalted power.<br /> <br /> The Dawn Caste represents the pursuit of human excellence in combat through the aesthetics of the Unconquered Sun in a manner that defines the upper boundary of Exalted power.<br /> <br /> The Zenith Caste represents the pursuit of human excellence in messianism through the aesthetics of the Unconquered Sun in a manner that defines the upper boundary of Exalted power.<br /> <br /> The Twilight Caste represents the pursuit of human excellence in scholarship through the aesthetics of the Unconquered Sun in a manner that defines the upper boundary of Exalted power.<br /> <br /> The Night Caste represents the pursuit of human excellence in furtiveness through the aesthetics of the Unconquered Sun in a manner that defines the upper boundary of Exalted power.<br /> <br /> The Eclipse Caste represents the pursuit of human excellence in diplomacy through the aesthetics of the Unconquered Sun in a manner that defines the upper boundary of Exalted power.<br /> <br /> (Yeah, most of those specializations suck, but I can\u2019t think of any better one-word summations of what each Caste does.)<br /> <br /> The purpose of the Castes is to provide a level of complexity that can be used as the foundation for a concrete a character concept. They\u2019re more precise and useful than the concept of Solars when writing up a character. They\u2019re also useful to introduce the concept of intra-splat divisions as a core piece of the setting.<br /> <br /> This leads to the final distinction:<br /> <br /> Distinction 4: Character/Caste<br /> <br /> These are the infinite distinctions that differentiate individual Solar characters from their Caste. As with Solars and the Exalted and Castes and Solars, the Castes include all characters of that Caste, but characters are not their Caste. While Solars are too broad a concept to base a character on, Castes are too narrow, so individual characters can use favoured abilities, intimacies and character background to differentiate themselves from their Caste.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s how you use binaries to think Solars through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T17:07:19-08:00","id":18034,"title":"","content":"... you have no idea how many bad memories you have just reminded me...<br /> <br /> but still, well done :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T22:43:15-08:00","id":18191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/18028-binary-thinking-solars-and-you#post18028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All thinking is fundamentally binary \u2013 a thing is itself and not any other thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait. When did this happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T22:55:57-08:00","id":18196,"title":"","content":"01010111011010000110000101110100001111110010000001 00100100100000011001000110111101101110001001110111 01000010000001100101011101100110010101101110001011 100010111000101110<br /> <br /> 01011001011011110111010100100000011010110110111001 10010101110111001000000111010001101000011010010111 00110010000001110111011000010111001100100000011001 11011011110110100101101110011001110010000001110100 01101111001000000110100001100001011100000111000001 1001010110111000101110","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T03:49:14-08:00","id":18329,"title":"","content":"&quot;When Bodhisattva Avalokitesvara practiced the deep Prajnaparamita, she saw that the five skandhas were empty; thus he overcame all ills and suffering.<br /> <br /> &quot;O Sariputra! Form does not differ from the void, and the void does not differ from the form. Form is the void, and the void is form. The same is true for feelings, conceptions, impulses and consciousness.<br /> <br /> O Sariputra, the characteristics of the void is not created, not annihilated, not impure, not pure, not increasing, not decreasing.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/93-xegek","name":"Xegek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar93_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T04:22:06-08:00","id":18343,"title":"","content":"Eh, I'm in the camp that not all thinking is binary, or at least that some thinking is so finely graded as to be non-binary.<br /> <br /> On the other hand I like how this is written up as a way to more clearly define each exalt type. However it falls a bit apart when you get to charms like Seven Year Swarm Volley, which are pretty clearly solar charms in the DB charmset, but without the &quot;The Solar Exalted have a similar charm...&quot; text at the bottom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T04:32:57-08:00","id":18350,"title":"","content":"You know, I was thinking jokingly of an &quot;Our Exalts are Different&quot; TV Tropes page, but that got to me thinking in actual serious terms.<br /> <br /> I think a &quot;consistent definition of Exalted&quot; is a lot like a consistent definition of vampires.<br /> <br /> And not just in terms of different takes on vampires across different works of fiction, because I can think of at least two settings in which there are multiple beings, some of which are quite different, that are all called vampires, including our very own World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Like, even the Kindred are implied to be a variety of different beings with different origins who have certain points of similarity as a matter of coincidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T08:01:28-08:00","id":19737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ithle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/18028-binary-thinking-solars-and-you?p=18191#post18191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait. When did this happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell if I know. I mean, Tiresias isn't even talking about binaries for the most part, he's talking about sub-groups within larger groups, which are not the same thing. A binary is a duality, where it is either one thing or the other, and cannot possibly be something else: a light switch is either on or off, it is either day or night, a man is either alive or dead, and so on.<br /> <br /> The only case Tiresias presents that is actually a duality is Exalted/Non-Exalted. Beyond that, he's just talking about distinctions among sub-groups: if Solars/Exalted was actually a binary, then one could only be a Solar or some generic Exalted, rather than being one of the other many, many types of Exalted. The same goes for the castes, unless there are suddenly only two Castes in the entire Solar splat, and I'm not even getting into the character variations that are possible within a caste.<br /> <br /> Besides, I'm not even sure what the <i>point</i> of this is. Is it arguing against the idea of a sliding scale of Exalted-ness? Because if it's ambiguity that's the problem, and an inability to distinguish where one thing begins and another ends, then the light spectrum must give you conniptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T19:53:57-08:00","id":20477,"title":"","content":"&quot;What? I don't even...You knew this was going to happen.&quot; is what <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex\">Arteliex</a> </b><b>was saying..lol</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/238-hammerofheaven","name":"HammerofHeaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar238_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T20:11:46-08:00","id":20479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/18028-binary-thinking-solars-and-you#post18028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All thinking is fundamentally binary \u2013 a thing is itself and not any other thing. The trick is defining what the thing is and what it isn\u2019t and determining how a thing is marked as itself and not any other thing. In other words, how do you define the binary distinction?</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything that exists has a specific nature, each entity exists as something in particular and has characteristics that are part of what it is. &quot;A&quot; is &quot;A&quot;. And no matter what reality he calls home, &quot;Luthor&quot; is &quot;Luthor&quot;. If I'm to save the world, your existence must come to an end, before you take office.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T13:31:29-08:00","id":20762,"title":"","content":"Binary thinking can be a good thing at times, but the implication that it's the core of all thinking seems excessive to me. There's as much room in the foundations of intelligence and reason for continuums as there is for discrete collections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T14:40:52-08:00","id":20801,"title":"","content":"Goddamn, quoting two posts is a pain in the ass.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ithle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/18028-binary-thinking-solars-and-you?p=18191#post18191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait. When did this happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since language was invented. A word is either correct or it isn't. If it isn't correct, you try a different word. That's basically what language boils down to.<br /> <br /> This causes significant problems when two people with different frames of reference try to communicate, but that's not really important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/18028-binary-thinking-solars-and-you?p=19737#post19737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hell if I know. I mean, Tiresias isn't even talking about binaries for the most part, he's talking about sub-groups within larger groups, which are not the same thing. A binary is a duality, where it is either one thing or the other, and cannot possibly be something else: a light switch is either on or off, it is either day or night, a man is either alive or dead, and so on.<br /> <br /> The only case Tiresias presents that is actually a duality is Exalted/Non-Exalted. Beyond that, he's just talking about distinctions among sub-groups: if Solars/Exalted was actually a binary, then one could only be a Solar or some generic Exalted, rather than being one of the other many, many types of Exalted. The same goes for the castes, unless there are suddenly only two Castes in the entire Solar splat, and I'm not even getting into the character variations that are possible within a caste.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a gap between abstract conceptualization and practical application of game concepts that I haven't been able to resolve to my satisfaction, probably because I can't find the correct words.<br /> <br /> It's like... if there were two Castes, you could get a distinction of Dawn/Zenith for the combat and the social Caste and that would work. However, because there are 5 Castes, it's impossible to set that up as a binary, so you need to set up a system where 1) all of the Castes are independent of each other and 2) all the Castes differentiate themselves from the same thing because, fundamentally, they're all <i>Solar</i> Castes and must have something in common.<br /> <br /> So you get Dawn/Solar, Zenith/Solar, Twilight/Solar, Night/Solar and Eclipse/Solar and those work as binaries because they're all independent of each other, including the concept of Solars.<br /> <br /> In the distinction of Solar/Exalted, the concept of &quot;Exalted&quot; has no inherent ontology. It's constructed by the concept of &quot;Solar&quot; and exists for the sole purpose of defining the concept of &quot;Solar&quot; and the criteria that are and aren't part of &quot;Solars.&quot; The concept of &quot;Solar&quot; constitutes itself in contrast to the Exalted in general, defining itself through the characteristics of &quot;Solar&quot; that are not part of the Exalted in general.<br /> <br /> In the distinction of, say, Dawn/Solar, it is the concept of &quot;Solar&quot; that has no ontology and that exists only so that the Dawn Caste can define itself. The distinctions of Solar/Exalted, Dawn/Solar, Zenith/Solar, Twilight/Solar, Night/Solar and Eclipse/Solar all use concepts of &quot;Solar&quot; that are theoretically unrelated to each other, despite being identical in practice.<br /> <br /> I thought about using a distinction of Caste/Other Castes but it just didn't seem right. I think it just makes more sense for the Castes to be defined in relation to Solars and I don't think the concept of &quot;Other Castes&quot; really works as a common point, but I can't quite figure out why.<br /> <br /> In any case, the utility of binary thinking here is that, when you make a Solar character, you only need to make five comparisons: Dawn/Solar, Zenith/Solar, Twilight/Solar, Night/Solar and Eclipse/Solar. Once you know how each Caste is different from Solars, you're good to go. If you want to tell the Castes apart from each other, you need to make 10 comparisons to get all the permutations. Binary thinking is twice as efficient.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/18028-binary-thinking-solars-and-you?p=19737#post19737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, I'm not even sure what the <i>point</i> of this is. Is it arguing against the idea of a sliding scale of Exalted-ness? Because if it's ambiguity that's the problem, and an inability to distinguish where one thing begins and another ends, then the light spectrum must give you conniptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>There really isn't one. It's just 40% me being pissed at people who think Castes don't matter (they're necessary in order to establish a level of specialization that isn't part of the Solar Exalted in general and is, in fact, antithetical to them as a splat), 40% me being pissed at people who think Getimians are Sidereals+ because they're both related to Fate somehow (which is a pointless comparison both because similarities between the two don't matter and because Getimians have to differentiate themselves from all Exalted at the same time, not just Sidereals) and 20% boredom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T16:31:18-08:00","id":20855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/18028-binary-thinking-solars-and-you?p=20801#post20801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Goddamn, quoting two posts is a pain in the ass.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Since language was invented. A word is either correct or it isn't. If it isn't correct, you try a different word. That's basically what language boils down to.<br /> <br /> This causes significant problems when two people with different frames of reference try to communicate, but that's not really important.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As someone with a background in the physical sciences I'll just have to take your word for it, but the whole thing seems absolutely ridiculous to me because of my education. I'd also disagree about the different frame of reference thing being unimportant because that seems pretty relevant to what you want to achieve here.<br /> <br /> However, I absolutely agree about the quoting two posts thing, that is a huge pain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T16:45:08-08:00","id":20859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/18028-binary-thinking-solars-and-you?p=20801#post20801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since language was invented. A word is either correct or it isn't. If it isn't correct, you try a different word. That's basically what language boils down to.<br /> <br /> This causes significant problems when two people with different frames of reference try to communicate, but that's not really important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Continuing my trend of only engaging with abstract navel-gazing topics peripheral to the point, I disagree with this! Words don't have a universal, objective meaning, and even if they did that meaning would at best only describe something like a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prototype_theory\" target=\"_blank\">semantic prototype</a>. The suitability of a word isn't just continuous, it's continuous on multiple dimensions. There have been some attempts to enforce an artificial objective precision on language, but they tend to be brittle and of little use in day-to-day life.<br /> <br /> (I get the feeling that what you're talking about is partly the use of discrete <i>models</i> for heuristic purposes, which is a different kettle of fish. I'm generally fine with the use of models so long as they're kept at arms' length and treated as models. But it's more fun to debate highly rarefied semantic and epistemological issues.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T16:57:56-08:00","id":20868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ithle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/18028-binary-thinking-solars-and-you?p=20855#post20855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone with a background in the physical sciences I'll just have to take your word for it, but the whole thing seems absolutely ridiculous to me because of my education. I'd also disagree about the different frame of reference thing being unimportant because that seems pretty relevant to what you want to achieve here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it's important, just not in this particular case. It's mostly an issue when you have two people speaking different languages, or speaking the same languages, but using words that take on different meanings in different regions or using technical jargon that varies from one field to other or something of that order.<br /> <br /> For example, what I meant to say is that frame of reference is not important to what I'm discussing in this thread, not that it's <i>never</i> important. If you're dealing with external communication, there's no right or wrong way to produce or interpret it, just different constructions. If you are dealing with internal communication, which uses a single frame of reference, then you have to be consistent or else it becomes impossible to determine whether words are being applied correctly or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T19:11:05-08:00","id":20928,"title":"","content":"(...seems this forum has some serious problems with nested quotes. That's a huge step down from the previous engine)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/18028-binary-thinking-solars-and-you?p=20801#post20801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since language was invented. A word is either correct or it isn't. If it isn't correct, you try a different word. That's basically what language boils down to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely untrue, It's an idea, but in reality that kind of perfectly precise language simply does not exist. Languages try to enforce a frame of reference onto the observed world, trying to present it in concrete definitions, but it's an inherently flawed method. The definitions of the words are always fuzzy and indistinct, unless the concepts those words represent are highly precise (and usually artificial) constructs.<br /> Just pick any word, and try to see the border between &quot;it&quot; and &quot;not-it&quot;. You will realize that (with the few special exceptions mentioned above) that border is not that clearly defined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":434,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","user":"Astralporing","date":". 11-30-2013, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T20:12:52-08:00","id":20957,"title":"","content":"If language was so binary, we wouldn't be able to use metaphors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T00:27:24-08:00","id":21034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/18028-binary-thinking-solars-and-you?p=20868#post20868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, it's important, just not in this particular case. It's mostly an issue when you have two people speaking different languages, or speaking the same languages, but using words that take on different meanings in different regions or using technical jargon that varies from one field to other or something of that order.<br /> <br /> For example, what I meant to say is that frame of reference is not important to what I'm discussing in this thread, not that it's <i>never</i> important. If you're dealing with external communication, there's no right or wrong way to produce or interpret it, just different constructions. If you are dealing with internal communication, which uses a single frame of reference, then you have to be consistent or else it becomes impossible to determine whether words are being applied correctly or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYeah, which is why it's important here. RPGs are filled with inconsistent technical jargon as well as misappropriated or misused words and Exalted certainly has its share of all of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T03:10:40-08:00","id":21087,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of different stuff being discussed here, so I'll jump in and see how many branches I can hit on the way down.<br /> <br /> <b>1. Thought is not primarily linguistic in nature</b> - While some people my think about things in terms of an inner monologue or dialogue, there's still a huge amount of mental activity doesn't involve words at all. Nor is language our primary means of experiencing the world around us. Language is a tool of communication, and while how you communicate and what you're limited in communicating influences your thinking, 'Language is binary so thinking is binary' grossly overestimates the amount of influence language has while ignoring all the other factors.<br /> <br /> <b>2. Language is rather non-binary</b> - A word is a loose grab back of mutually agreed upon definitions, and that might be the simplest part of language. You can use the same word to mean different things 'I drank a can of pop,' 'I heard a pop from my neck,' and 'Pop goes the weasel.' You can use a 'wrong' word and people will know exactly what you mean. Children do this all the time: 'I want to play with choo-choo.' 'I want to drink my fizzy.' 'Can I pet the furry?'<br /> <br /> That adults call trains 'trains' instead of choo-choo isn't an expression of how we think; the human mind perceives an object as a collection of associated elements, so identifying something by a unique sound - 'choo-choo' - is more natural than an unrelated identifier until you've spent enough time calling these things trains and hearing them referred to as trains that 'trainness' become a conceptual category in its own right.<br /> <br /> Rather, that sort of standardization is imposed by society and a desire for strong, clear communication among millions of people. Even then, try to get five different people to agree on the correct definition for the word 'good.'<br /> <br /> If you take this to the sentence level, your immediate problem is sarcasm. A slight change in my tone can turn the sentence 'That was a good idea' from a compliment to an insult. But the listener/reader can only guess as to how genuine I am in what I'm saying. 'That was a good idea' is an ambiguous statement, even though on a structural level, it's perfectly clear English.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 12-01-2013, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T03:23:50-08:00","id":21094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/18028-binary-thinking-solars-and-you?p=18196#post18196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">01010111011010000110000101110100001111110010000001 00100100100000011001000110111101101110001001110111 01000010000001100101011101100110010101101110001011 100010111000101110<br /> <br /> 01011001011011110111010100100000011010110110111001 10010101110111001000000111010001101000011010010111 00110010000001110111011000010111001100100000011001 11011011110110100101101110011001110010000001110100 01101111001000000110100001100001011100000111000001 1001010110111000101110</div> </div> </div> </div>01010011011000010110010001101100011110010010111000 10111000101110001000000111100101100101011100110010 1110","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}